        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-23 01:09:18.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20726 tests: restore at_max after sanity test_401dc",
        "message": "LU-20726 tests: restore at_max after sanity test_401dc\n\nsanity test_401dc raises at_max by 10 with \"set_param -P\", and its\ncleanup set at_max back with \"set_param -P\" without waiting for the\nclients to apply it.  The change reaches the client only after its\nconfig lock is revoked and the params llog is reprocessed, so the\nnext tests could start with the raised at_max.  test_401gb would\nthen save the raised value, remount the client, which applied the\nrestored at_max from the params llog, and fail with:\n\n    at_max not 610, got 600\n\nThe cleanup also left an at_max record in the params llog, so every\nlater remount in the session applied it.\n\nDelete the at_max records from the params llog first, so no node\napplies them on a later llog reprocess, then set the original\nat_max directly on all nodes before the test returns, since\ndeleting the records does not change the value on the nodes.\n\nDrop the default EXIT argument from the test's stack_trap calls.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: c4020bb2b4c1 (\"LU-20726 obdclass: validate parameter names in config\")\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Ia9344e300afe1b304e63b7558244624f533ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
